===Poland vs Ecuador===
Poland and Ecuador had previously met once before their opening World Cup match, playing out a 1–1 draw during a [[Exhibition match|friendly]] in November 2005.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/poland/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Ecuador/ |title=Poland national football team: record v Ecuador |website=11v11.com |publisher=AFS Enterprises|accessdate=4 January 2023}}</ref> The Poles pressed the attack for the opening 20 minutes of the match, but were unable to create any significant chances. 24 minutes in, Ecuador took the lead when [[Carlos Tenorio]] got ahead of [[Marcin Baszczyński]] to head in after teammate [[Agustín Delgado]] had nodded the ball towards him from a long throw.<ref name="PolEcu">{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2006/4852548.stm |title=Poland 0–2 Ecuador|work=BBC Sport |date=9 June 2006 |access-date=4 January 2023}}</ref><ref name="g2">{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2006/jun/10/worldcup2006.sport31 |title=Delgado proves a saint for Ecuador with a flick and a strike to finish Poland |newspaper=The Guardian|last=Brodkin |first=Jon |date=10 June 2006 |accessdate=7 January 2023}}</ref> Tenorio became only the third player to have scored a World Cup goal for Ecuador after Delgado and [[Édison Méndez]]. Buoyed by their goal, Ecuador took control of the game and had several chances before the end of the first half but failed to convert.<ref name="PolEcu"/> However, Poland had struggled to make an impression and Jon Brodkin of ''The Guardian'' noted that they had "forced not a single meaningful save" from the opposition goalkeeper.<ref name="g2"/> 

In the second half, Poland began pushing forward with [[Mirosław Szymkowiak]] creating several near chances, the best of which sent [[Jacek Krzynówek]] through before being called offside.<ref name="g2"/> In the final third of the game, Poland were denied by the woodwork twice; first when [[Ireneusz Jeleń]] struck the crossbar with a shot and later when [[Paweł Brożek]] hit the post. Despite their attacking threat, it was Ecuador who were able to score when [[Iván Kaviedes]] broke through before laying the ball off for Delgado to give his side a 2–0 lead.<ref name="PolEcu"/> Delgado's goal made him his country's record World Cup goalscorer, which he would remain until being surpassed by [[Enner Valencia]] at the [[2022 FIFA World Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.11v11.com/matches/qatar-v-ecuador-20-november-2022-376095/ |title=Qatar v Ecuador, 20 November 2022 |website=11v11.com |publisher=AFS Enterprises |accessdate=4 January 2023}}</ref> This match was the fifth consecutive time that Poland had failed to score in their opening match at a World Cup finals.<ref name="PolEcu"/>

