==Aftermath==
[[File:FIFA WC-qualification 2014 - Austria vs. Germany 2012-09-11 - Miroslav Klose 01.JPG|upright|thumb|[[Miroslav Klose]] scored four times for Germany in Group A]]
Germany finished top of the group with nine points having won all three of their group matches. They faced [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]], the runners-up of [[2006 FIFA World Cup Group B|Group B]], in the round of 16, winning 2–0.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2006/4991466.stm |title=Germany 2–0 Sweden |work=BBC Sport |date=24 June 2006 |access-date=5 January 2023}}</ref> They went on to defeat [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] in the quarter-finals on penalties before suffering defeat to [[Italy national football team|Italy]] in the semi-finals. Germany finished third after defeating [[Portugal national football team|Portugal]] 3–1 in the match for third place.<ref name="bracket">{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2006germany |title=2006 FIFA World Cup |publisher=FIFA |accessdate=5 January 2023}}</ref> As runners-up in the group with six points, Ecuador faced the winners of Group B, [[England national football team|England]], in the next round but were eliminated after a 1–0 defeat.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2006/4991536.stm |title=England 1–0 Ecuador |work=BBC Sport |date=25 June 2006 |access-date=5 January 2023}}</ref> Poland would not return to the competition until the [[2018 FIFA World Cup|2018 World Cup]] while Costa Rica failed to qualify for the [[2010 FIFA World Cup|2010 World Cup]] before returning for the [[2014 FIFA World Cup|2014 tournament]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/polands-world-cup-history-2022-133107049.html?src=rss&guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAANMOqNexFto8jLU99qq4Zxtg0sdPW9Pwpv0EATnpipwJixchnPZfKjCsfvM9FWd26Z3YARoD7F_3h37NEwBE4_7zg9Tv-xaLgfBZOYGSALmdUCIYurhXq7FSwjI5aqIMGjSjWTp9A3CrWevAWOG-KEJRnHoZ-K0_Zvx4c5osUBLG |title=Poland's World Cup History Before 2022 FIFA Tournament |publisher=Yahoo Sports |last=Molski |first=Max |date=22 November 2022 |accessdate=5 January 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/sport/football/2022/jun/14/costa-rica-new-zealand-to-play-off-for-last-fifa-world-cup-place-2465452.html |title=Costa Rica, New Zealand to play off for last FIFA World Cup place |newspaper=The New Indian Express |date=14 June 2022 |accessdate=5 January 2023}}</ref>

Klose's four goals during the group stage contributed to him winning the [[World Cup Golden Boot|Golden Boot]] as the competition's top goalscorer. He finished the World Cup with five in total,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/football/top-stories/world-cup-top-scorer-miroslav-klose-calls-it-a-day/articleshow/40096669.cms |title=World Cup top goalscorer Miroslav Klose calls it a day |newspaper=The Times of India |last=Basu |first=Saumyajit |date=12 August 2014 |access-date=5 January 2023}}</ref> the lowest tally needed to win the award since [[1962 FIFA World Cup|1962]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://olympics.com/en/news/fifa-world-cup-golden-boot-winners-top-goal-scorers |title=FIFA World Cup Golden Boot winners: Top goal scorers from each edition |publisher=International Olympic Committee|last=Nag |first=Utathya |date=18 December 2022 |accessdate=9 January 2023}}</ref> His teammate Podolski went on to win the young player of the tournament award.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/fifaplus/en/watch/2MAxnPKIwA6ImJt6ATRte6#:~:text=Close%20Share-,Lukas%20Podolski%20%7C%20Best%20Young%20Player%20Award%20%7C%202006,FIFA%20World%20Cup%20Germany%E2%84%A2&text=1min%2020second-,The%20Hyundai%20Best%20Young%20Player%20Award%20is%20given%20to%20the,winner%20on%20FIFA's%20official%20website. |title=Lukas Podolski Best Young Player |publisher=FIFA|date=25 August 2006|accessdate=9 January 2023}}</ref>

